  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nShowers and thunderstorms through mid-afternoon\n\nLeading edge of 850mb warm advection has led to showers and \nthunderstorms developing in northeast Iowa with these shifting into \nsouthwest Wisconsin early this afternoon. Expect these to continue \nto progress east of our area over the next couple hours. Without \nmuch time for the surface boundary layer to become well mixed, am \nnot expecting strong or severe wind gusts and, with weak deep layer \nshear ahead of the warm advection, am not concerned with hail either.\n\nBreezy Saturday, record warmth possible\n\nDeepening surface low pressure in SK/MB will lead to an increase in \n850mb winds over the region and a tightening surface pressure \ngradient. This, coupled with mostly clear skies and efficient \nmixing, will lead to breezy conditions across the CWA. For our usual \nwindy spots in southeast Minnesota outside the Mississippi Valley, \nthere is still a chance (30-40% per 09.12z REFS and 09.13z NBM) for \na 45 mph gust, a bit lower than runs yesterday as the strongest \n850mb winds have trended northwest of the area. Have therefore \nrefrained from issuing a Wind Advisory.\n\nThese southwesterly winds will also bring notably warmer air to the \nregion with highs in the mid 80s and low 80s Saturday and Sunday, \nrespectively. Should temperatures overachieve by just a couple \ndegrees Saturday, new record highs for the date would be set, as \ndetailed in the Climate section below.\n\nRain likely next week but timing uncertain\n\nGuidance in strong agreement that a strong upper low will barrel \neastward over southern Nevada and progress northeast to the Upper \nMidwest. However, significant (+/- 1 day) timing differences are \nseen across ensemble guidance and therefore, while the chance for \nprecip occurring sometime during mid to late next week is high (80%) \nthe forecast carries 30-60% mentions of precipitation from Tuesday \nnight through Thursday night. Expect these PoPs to eventually focus \non a shorter time period and become higher in future updates. \nProgged 850mb temperatures may (20-30%) drop below 0C as the core of \nthe upper low passes but 925mb and surface temps should remain above \nfreezing, so this looks to be an all rain event.",
